==Strategy==
==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
This stage is more time consuming than difficult as Elizabeth the LVIth is more of a massive tank and less of a wave breaker, kind of like [[Kory]].

Still, you should be prepared to deal with plenty of Peons and the Queen herself. Meatshields are worth less than normal in this stage as Queen Pig will just chew through them anyway. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] are enough for this stage in Chapter 1. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] or [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Thor Cat]] will help if you own them as their DPS is quite good and they can be subbed in for Wall Cat.

If you have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or any Cat with the [[Wave Shield]] or [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] [[Special Abilities|ability]], bring them along, as they make this battle much easier. Even with very few [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] this stage will be doable in Chapter 1, it will just be time consuming.

You probably won't have any [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] [[True Form]]s at this point. In any case, just use [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan/Jamiera]] against the pig, Elizabeth the LVIth. Make sure you have all of your [[treasure]]s from [[Empire of Cats Levels (EN)|Empire of Cats]]. Also make sure you have as many [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures|anti-Alien treasures]] as you can. It is also useful to get True Forms of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]] and [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Viking Cat]] but it is possible with Artist Cat and Thor Cat. Add [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] if you have it or you can use Solar Cat.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
You should max out your worker and wallet at the beginning of this stage.

All Chapter 3 adds is Metal Doges, but they do change the battle quite a lot if you are unprepared. Use a modified strategy with [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]]. If you're having trouble staying alive against the [[Elizabeth the LVIth|Elizabeth]] waves and you don't yet have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or a wave shield, Bring your most powerful Anti-alien team and spam [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cats]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs]], and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cats]].

Occasionally spawn [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie]] if you can to try for a freeze. You can try your luck with spawning [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway]] cat, but this is very luck dependent on if the wave comes out and if your unit will freeze.

Weaker meatshields like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] will die in one wave hit, so don't even spawn them in until the Elizabeth the LVIth defeats. If you don't have many units, it might be worth bringing a Unit Defense Up, Unit Attack Up, or Strong Against/Resistant combos to help out your anti-Alien units.

